  "abstract": "Following the SOTA success of the 4-ramp MoLR v1 (ID 475) and its analysis (ID 479), this experiment is an ablation study on the number of ramp archetypes. I am reducing the number of learned ramps from 4 to 2. The goal is to determine if the diversity of the four learned strategies is essential for performance. Based on the visualization of the 4 distinct learned ramps, I hypothesize that this reduction in complexity will lead to a lower score. All other hyperparameters and the BASE_SEED are fixed for a controlled comparison.",
